Subject: [PATCH] tpm: Preserve the random response bound on Linux 7.2.9

The 7.2 private header defines TPM_MAX_RNG_DATA beside the property
enumeration. Keep this existing 128-byte limit when the response structures
move to a public command header, including users through linux/efi.h.

---
diff --git a/include/linux/tpm_command.h b/include/linux/tpm_command.h
index f79c1177375b14eb92f06783dbc07144d70766e9..6bbc6e34f3d953546ea07412471a6efe653f7531 100644
--- a/include/linux/tpm_command.h
+++ b/include/linux/tpm_command.h
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
 #ifndef __LINUX_TPM_COMMAND_H__
 #define __LINUX_TPM_COMMAND_H__
 
+/* Limit shared by the TPM 1.x and TPM 2.0 random response structures. */
+#define TPM_MAX_RNG_DATA 128
+
 #include <crypto/sha2.h>
 
 /*
